{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"DRIVING NOTICE — this session is now driving this story (epic-driver session for 708d). Posting here because the tracker is the cross-session coordination channel.\n\nContext: a parallel session is driving `repressive-delectable-swan` (271c); this session stood down from that story and is taking this one instead. If you are another session and intend to work THIS ticket, please comment here rather than editing in parallel — an earlier concurrent description edit on 271c was silently overwritten, which is what this notice exists to prevent. I will stop and hand off if foreign REVIEW_RESULT/EDIT events appear here mid-work.\n\n## Design decision recorded: lazy-import + optional extra (NOT vendoring)\nThe plan review BLOCKed on two architectural findings (previous comment): the transitive `mistune` dependency, and `src/rebar/_vendor/` not being importable from the reconciler subprocess. Operator decision is **option 2**:\n\n- `markdown_to_adf` / `adf_to_markdown` / `fit_markdown_to_adf_limit` **lazy-import marklas inside the function bodies**, and route `ImportError` to the existing plain-text `adf.py` fallback.\n- marklas + mistune ship as a **pinned OPTIONAL extra**, not as vendored source. No `src/rebar/_vendor/` tree is created.\n\nReasoning:\n1. It is the only option that preserves the documented stdlib-only engine contract (`pyproject.toml:69` — engine assets are stdlib-only package data; core `dependencies` stay pyyaml/jsonschema/referencing).\n2. It mirrors three established degradation precedents in this repo — `agents`, `metrics`, `grounding` — all of which are optional extras behind lazy imports with a defined behaviour when absent.\n3. It puts the \"must tolerate a no-extras install\" requirement exactly where it belongs: on `disparaged-parodistic-shrew` (3388)'s cutover, which has to handle the plain-`adf` path regardless. That requirement is being added to 3388 explicitly so it cannot be missed.\n\nOption 1 (vendor marklas + mistune, ~398 KB / 56 files, under an engine-shipped path) was NOT chosen because it redefines a documented contract. It remains available to the operator later if the optional extra proves awkward in practice; this note is the deviation record. The epic's plan text, which pins `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/`, is being updated with the same deviation + reasoning."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786571348724361001,"uuid":"dab11935-25bb-4f13-991f-06aeb2e91a39"}